# gpu_capture native addon — NOTHING under build/ is tracked. Shipped binaries live in
# prebuilds/<platform>-<arch>/ instead (written by `npm run build:native`).
#
# The reason a binary must be committed at all is real: CI never runs `npm run build:native` (ci.yml
# does `npm ci`, whose prepare script is tsc-only), so without one loadGpuCapture() finds nothing and
# the suite silently degrades from `shared`/`readback` capture to `direct` — green either way, which
# is precisely the failure this repo tries not to ship.
#
# But build/Release holds exactly ONE binary, for whichever machine last ran the build. That is
# present-but-unloadable on every other platform, which is strictly worse than absent: it produced a
# Linux run that reported NVENC only after a manual rebuild, and would silently invalidate any
# benchmark taken on a fresh non-macOS clone. Keying by platform-arch makes a foreign build
# unreachable rather than mis-loaded.
#
# One prebuild per platform+arch is sufficient for ALL Electron versions: the addon is pure N-API
# (node-addon-api, no raw v8), verified by loading an Electron-43 build inside plain Node 22 (ABI 148
# vs 147). It is NOT ABI-pinned, so an Electron bump does not invalidate prebuilds.
#
# Everything else under build/ is node-gyp / @electron/rebuild scratch — Makefiles, config.gypi,
# .deps and .o files — that bakes in an absolute path to whatever worktree last built it, so it
# churns every diff and is regenerable in one command. bin/ is @electron/rebuild's per-ABI cache.
src/render/native/electron/native/build/
src/render/native/electron/native/bin/
